IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT domain
IMPORT `g2-nouns`
IMPORT `g2-readings`
IMPORT `g2-fixtures`
IMPORT `g2-art3-4-commissioner`
IMPORT `g2-art6-purposes`
IMPORT `g2-art7-public-benefit`
IMPORT `g2-art5-charity-test`

-- g2-tests-red.l4: assertions that are MEANT to fail, and counted: 15 in all, so `check-g2.sh` expects exactly 15 failed assertions here and no other error.
-- Fourteen of them state, under the FAVOURED interpretation, the answer that the OTHER reading of a fork would give.  Each therefore fails exactly because the fork is real: the two readings
-- differ on that case, and the group takes the first.  (The fork register in FRAGMENT-G2.md names the discriminating case; the green tests in the other g2-tests modules assert both answers
-- under the reading that gives each.)  The fifteenth is a control: an assertion that cannot hold, which shows that this harness reports a failure when there is one.
-- Do not "fix" an assertion in this file by editing its expected value: each is red on purpose.

§ `Assertions that are meant to fail`

GIVETH A `Determination of public benefit`
`a determination by the Commissioner that presumes a charitable purpose` MEANS
    `a determination that provides public benefit by presuming a charitable purpose to be for the public benefit, made by` `the Commissioner`

§§ `Control`

-- The control: 1 does not equal 2.
#ASSERT 1 EQUALS 2

§§ `Each fork, answered as its other reading answers it`

-- F2.1: an entity with no purposes.  The second and third readings say it satisfies 5(1)(a); the favoured first reading says it does not.
#ASSERT `Art 5(1)(a) all of the entity's purposes are charitable or purely ancillary` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7` (`a G2 entity with these purposes` EMPTY) EMPTY

-- F2.1: an ancillary purpose alone.  The third reading accepts it; the favoured first reading does not.
#ASSERT `Art 5(1)(a) all of the entity's purposes are charitable or purely ancillary` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7` (`a G2 entity with these purposes` (LIST `a G2 ancillary purpose`)) (LIST (`the G2 purpose` `a G2 ancillary purpose` `with` `G2 facts: nothing relevant`))

-- F2.2: a sitting member of the States Assembly may be a trustee in a personal capacity.  The second reading says the constitution is within 5(2); the favoured first reading says it is not.
#ASSERT `Art 5(2) the constitution defeats the charity test` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7` `the Chief Minister` (`a G2 constitution that expressly permits` `any of the governors of the entity to be` `by` `a member of the States Assembly` `with the capacity` FALSE)

-- F2.3: the constitution permits the Minister for Health to be a governor.  The second reading says it is not within 5(2); the favoured first reading says it is.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 5(2) the constitution defeats the charity test` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7` `the Chief Minister` (`a G2 constitution that expressly permits` `any of the governors of the entity to be` `by` `a Minister who holds another ministerial office, the Minister for Health, say` `with the capacity` TRUE)

-- F2.4: guidance issued 1 January 2026, copy given 1 March 2026, N = 30, and the time held to be reasonable.  The second reading says it was late; the favoured first reading says it was in time.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 5(7) the Commissioner provided the Minister with the guidance and the report in time` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7` (YMD 2026 1 1) (JUST (YMD 2026 3 1)) TRUE 30

-- F2.5: a purpose of advancing a philosophical belief.  The second reading says it is within paragraph (1)(c); the favoured first reading says it is within (p) only.
#ASSERT `Art 6 the purpose is within the advancement of religion` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7` `a G2 purpose of advancing a philosophical belief`

-- F2.6: with days measured, the copy on 31 January for a guidance issued on 1 January and N = 30.  If the day of the event counts as the first day, that is late; the favoured reading counts from the day after.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 5(7) the Commissioner provided the Minister with the guidance and the report in time` `the interpretation of Articles 3 to 7 with F2.4 read as B` (YMD 2026 1 1) (JUST (YMD 2026 1 31)) FALSE 30

-- F2.7: the report published on the day the guidance is issued.  The second reading says that is before; the favoured first reading says it is not.
#ASSERT `Art 5(6) the consultation and the report preceded the guidance` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7` (YMD 2026 1 20) (JUST (YMD 2026 1 10)) (JUST (YMD 2026 1 20))

-- F2.8: assisting a foreign equivalent body where that assistance relates to no function.  The second reading says the Commissioner has power; the favoured first reading says not.
#ASSERT `Art 4(3) the Commissioner has power to do the listed example` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7` `assisting an equivalent body outside Jersey in the performance of its functions` FALSE FALSE

-- F2.9: the first limb practicable and not sought, the last limb not practicable.  The second reading says the standard did not bind; the favoured first reading says it was broken.
#ASSERT `Art 4(4) the Commissioner has sought to act as Article 4(4) requires` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7` (`How the Commissioner acted in performing a function` OF (`A limb of the standard of conduct in Article 4(4)` OF TRUE, FALSE), (`A limb of the standard of conduct in Article 4(4)` OF TRUE, TRUE), (`A limb of the standard of conduct in Article 4(4)` OF TRUE, TRUE), (`A limb of the standard of conduct in Article 4(4)` OF TRUE, TRUE), (`A limb of the standard of conduct in Article 4(4)` OF FALSE, FALSE))

-- F2.10: the Commissioner presumed a charitable purpose to be for the public benefit and found that the entity provides it.  The first reading refuses; asserting that it does NOT refuse fails.
#ASSERT REFUSED `Art 7 the entity provides public benefit` `the interpretation of Articles 3 to 7 with F2.10 read as B` (`a G2 entity with these purposes` EMPTY) `a determination by the Commissioner that presumes a charitable purpose`

-- F2.11: a purpose that promotes diversity but not equality.  The second reading says it is a charitable purpose under (l); the favoured first reading says it is not.
#ASSERT `Art 6(1) the purpose is a charitable purpose` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7` (`a G2 purpose recorded under` `the promotion of equality and diversity`) `G2 facts: diversity promoted, equality not`

-- F2.12: guidance on the duties of governors under 4(1)(d), on no 5(4) subject.  The second reading says Articles 5(6) to 5(8) apply to it; the favoured first reading says they do not.
#ASSERT `Art 5(6) Articles 5(6) to 5(8) apply to the guidance` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7` (LIST `the operation of the Law, including the duties of governors and the charity test`)

-- F2.13: a member of the Commissioner's staff, authorized under Schedule 1 paragraph 4(3), finds that an entity that benefits only one named natural person provides public benefit.  The second reading says the finding stands
-- (Article 7(1) names only the Commissioner, the tribunal and the court); the favoured first reading says 7(3)(b) binds the staff finding and the entity does not provide public benefit.
#ASSERT `Art 7 the entity provides public benefit` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7` (`a G2 entity with these purposes` EMPTY) (`a determination that provides public benefit for an entity that benefits only identified natural persons, made by` `a member of the Commissioner's staff`)
